# ============================================================
# vpn-stack environment (used by docker-compose.yaml)
#
# Local:     cp .env.example .env  and fill in the values
# Portainer: add the same variables under
#            Stacks -> vpn-stack -> Environment variables
#            (or use "Load variables from .env file")
#
# Never commit the real .env file.
# Keep comments on their own lines: some loaders do not strip
# inline comments and would put them inside the value.
#
# This stack has exactly one variable.
# ============================================================

# --- Tailscale ---
# Auth key from the Tailscale admin console:
#   Settings -> Keys -> Generate auth key
#
# Tick "Reusable" so the stack survives being re-created, and
# "Pre-approved" so the node does not wait for manual approval.
# The key starts with:  tskey-auth-
#
# It is readable with `docker inspect`, so prefer a reusable,
# ephemeral key with a short expiry and rotate it when this host
# is decommissioned.
TS_AUTHKEY=